Thank you for the update @danieldegrasse! I have tried to test with MCU mgr serial but that also results in a crash when I try to transfer. The exception is not consistent (similar to dfu-util transfer). Maybe you can use this information to find the root cause.

I test with this script:
```
#!/bin/bash

BOARD=mimxrt1050_evk

west build -b $BOARD -d build_mcuboot bootloader/mcuboot/boot/zephyr
west build -b $BOARD zephyr/samples/subsys/mgmt/mcumgr/smp_svr -- \
-DOVERLAY_CONFIG='overlay-serial.conf' -DCONFIG_BOOTLOADER_MCUBOOT=y \
'-DCONFIG_MCUBOOT_SIGNATURE_KEY_FILE="bootloader/mcuboot/root-rsa-2048.pem"'

west flash -d build_mcuboot
west flash

mcumgr --conntype serial --connstring "/dev/ttyUSB0,baud=115200" image list
mcumgr --conntype serial --connstring "/dev/ttyUSB0,baud=115200" image upload build/zephyr/zephyr.signed.bin
```

And I added these lines to `mimxrt1050_evk.dts `:
```
	chosen {
		zephyr,uart-mcumgr=&lpuart3;
```
```
&lpuart3 {
	status = "okay";
	current-speed = <115200>;
	pinctrl-0 = <&pinmux_lpuart3>;
	pinctrl-1 = <&pinmux_lpuart3_sleep>;
	pinctrl-names = "default", "sleep";
};
```
